diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ac4d8ce..9bd3a38 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -11,9 +11,19 @@ Rates depend on the destination zone and the parcel weight.
 | Zone | Code |
 | --- | --- |
 | Domestic | `DOM` |
-| Europe | `EU` |
+| Europe | `EUR` |
 | Rest of the world | `WW` |
 
+`shippingRate(weight, zone)` takes either a weight in kg or a shipment `{ weightKg, lengthCm, widthCm, heightCm }`. A shipment is priced by its chargeable weight, which `chargeableWeightKg(shipment)` returns:
+
+- The volumetric weight is `lengthCm × widthCm × heightCm / 5000`.
+- The chargeable weight is the larger of the actual and the volumetric weight, rounded up to the next 0.5 kg. A weight that is already a multiple of 0.5 kg stays as it is.
+- If any dimension is missing, the actual weight is used, still rounded up to 0.5 kg.
+
+For example, a 0.8 kg parcel measuring 40 × 30 × 20 cm has a volumetric weight of 4.8 kg and a chargeable weight of 5 kg.
+
+`shipmentsToCsv` lists both `weightKg` and `chargeableWeightKg` for each shipment and prices it by the chargeable weight.
+
 ## Delivery
 
 `estimateDelivery(orderedAt, transitDays)` returns the expected delivery date in Istanbul time.
